# Cloudflare Pages headers for the self-hosted TurboWarp editor.
# Drop this file (and _redirects, see README) into the Pages build output so the SPA serves correctly.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  # Do NOT set X-Frame-Options here: the KAT app must be able to frame this editor. Framing is controlled
  # by the KAT app's own CSP frame-src (see next.config.ts), which allow-lists this exact origin.

# Long-cache the fingerprinted build assets; the HTML entry stays uncached so deploys take effect.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# OPTIONAL: cross-origin isolation, only if you want TurboWarp's COMPILER / SharedArrayBuffer features.
# It is NOT required for the editor, the VM, or saving. It also makes every cross-origin subresource need
# CORP/CORS, which can break some extensions, so enable it deliberately, not by default.
# /*
#   Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
#   Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
